:: R3-GhostReaperDM [release3]
After the stream, I notice a DM in my Twitch inbox from GhostReaper42. I almost ignore it. Viewer DMs are usually either requests for free coaching, links to their own channels, or some variation of you should play this other game.

<div class="pt-phone">
<<phonehead "GhostReaper42" "Twitch DM" "G">>
<div class="pt-msg left">Hey man. Don't want to be weird but I've been watching you since you had like 2K followers. I can tell something's off lately. Your gameplay is fine but your energy is different. Not bad different. Just heavier. Anyway I re-upped my sub for 6 months. You're worth the investment. Just wanted you to know someone sees the real you behind the headset.</div>
</div>

I read it three times. Then a fourth time. My eyes sting and I hate that they do.

I type back, "That means more than you know. Seriously. Thank you."

Then I delete the seriously because it sounds too desperate. Then I add it back because it's true. Then I send it and close the laptop and sit in the dark for a minute.

GhostReaper42 has been subbed for nineteen consecutive months. He's sent maybe two hundred dollars in total donations over that period. I don't know his real name. I don't know what he looks like. He's a rectangular avatar and a username and two hundred dollars spread across nineteen months and somehow he just said the most perceptive thing anyone's said to me in weeks.

The real me behind the headset. What does that even look like anymore. I'm not sure the real me is someone worth investing in.

<hr class="pt-hr">

<div class="pt-choice-label">Reply To GhostReaper42</div>
<div class="pt-choices">
<<link "Send a genuine voice note thanking him" "R3-GhostReaper-Voice">><</link>>
<<link "Send a brief text reply, keep it light" "R3-GhostReaper-Text">><</link>>
<<link "Don't respond. Close the DM." "R3-GhostReaper-Ignore">><</link>>
</div>

